tence/checkpoints/{checkpoint_id}
POST /api/human-agent/persistence/checkpoint
POST /api/human-agent/persistence/assess
POST /api/human-agent/persistence/restoration-packet
POST /api/human-agent/persistence/handoff
```

Agent Bridge MCP tools:

```text
aura_checkpoint_session
aura_list_checkpoints
aura_restore_checkpoint
aura_fork_checkpoint
aura_handoff_checkpoint
```

The Coding Workbench exposes `checkpoint_state()`, `assess_checkpoint()`, `restoration_packet()`, and `list_checkpoints()` on its guarded session object.

A handoff packet is a payload-free digital baton. It identifies the source checkpoint, target Arena, payload digest, and required restoration gate; it does not mutate the target Arena. `TEMP:STALE` and `TEMP:BRANCH_OFFSET` force refresh/re-verification. Checkpoints are operational continuity records, not automatic authority or legal certification.

"""
    insert_before(
        path,
        "## 10. Cost and benchmark interpretation\n",
        section,
        "## 10. Temporal persistence and cross-Arena handoff",
    )
    replace_once(path, "## 10. Cost and benchmark interpretation\n", "## 11. Cost and benchmark interpretation\n")
    replace_once(path, "## 11. Testing\n", "## 12. Testing\n")
    replace_once(path, "## 12. Troubleshooting\n", "## 13. Troubleshooting\n")
    replace_once(path, "## 13. Safety rules\n", "## 14. Safety rules\n")


def patch_agent_bridge_doc() -> None:
    path = "docs/AURA_AGENT_ARENA_BRIDGE.md"
    replace_once(
        path,
        "| `aura_export_icm` | Export arena transaction into ICM audit workspace |\n",
        "| `aura_export_icm` | Export arena transaction into ICM audit workspace |\n"
        "| `aura_checkpoint_session` | Persist the prepared bridge session as a verifier-bound checkpoint |\n"
        "| `aura_list_checkpoints` | List checkpoint metadata without payloads |\n"
        "| `aura_restore_checkpoint` | Assess restore against current HEAD and invariants; never auto-apply |\n"
        "| `aura_fork_checkpoint` | Create a named what-if child checkpoint |\n"
        "| `aura_handoff_checkpoint` | Create a payload-free digital baton for another Arena |\n",
    )
    section = """## Temporal Persistence Tools

The MCP server uses `PersistentAuraAgentArenaBridge`, which extends the existing bridge without changing patch authority.

```text
prepare / stage / verify
  → aura_checkpoint_session
  → optional aura_fork_checkpoint
  → aura_restore_checkpoint
  → existing verifier and human review
```

A restore result is an assessment packet only. It cannot apply a patch, promote a hotswap, commit, push, open a PR, merge, or authorize a physical action. Cross-Arena handoff excludes the checkpoint payload by default.

"""
    insert_before(
        path,
        "## Example Codex CLI Workflow\n",
        section,
        "## Temporal Persistence Tools",
    )


def patch_handoff_log() -> None:
    path = "docs/AURA_CROSS_ARENA_CHANGE_HANDOFF_LOG.md"
    section = """

## Phase 4 temporal-persistence handoff

```yaml
baseline_main: c77e6d6558b2ee4f4c7f7c9160eff16e8ec0e4c5
active_branch: refactor/sco-construction-persistence-e9-e12
current_phase: E9_E12_TEMPORAL_PERSISTENCE
current_status: IMPLEMENTING
coderabbit_policy: TRIGGER_ONCE_AFTER_FINAL_MANUAL_AND_EXECUTABLE_GATES
```

| Capability | Canonical owner | Disposition |
|---|---|---|
| Content-addressed checkpoint and registry | `aura_temporal_persistence.py` | `NEW_GENERIC_OWNER` |
| Temporal stale/branch guard | `aura_wfst_temporal_adapter.py` | `NEW_NARROW_ADAPTER`; no active grammar mutation |
| Coding/Human/Bridge/Construction projections | `aura_arena_persistence_adapters.py` | `INTEGRATED` |
| Agent Bridge persistence MCP | `aura_agent_arena_persistence_bridge.py`, `aura_agent_arena_mcp.py` | `INTEGRATED` |
| Human Agent persistence API | `aura_human_agent_arena_server.py` | `INTEGRATED` |
| Automatic restore or hotswap | none | `FORBIDDEN` |
| Legal immutability/court admissibility | none | `NOT_CLAIMED` |
"""
    text = read(path)
    if "## Phase 4 temporal-persistence handoff" not in text:
        write(path, text.rstrip() + section.rstrip() + "\n")


def main() -> None:
    patch_state_ledger_facade()
    patch_coding_workbench()
    patch_human_agent_server()
    patch_agent_mcp()
    patch_readme()
    patch_architecture()
    patch_user_guide()
    patch_agent_bridge_doc()
    patch_handoff_log()


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
